From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:11:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iommu: rockchip: Add
 rockchip,disable-device-link-resume

The RK3528 VOP's IOMMU answers register reads only once the VOP has
turned its aclk pre auto gating off, so it must not be enabled on the
runtime resume that precedes the VOP's probe. Let a node say so; the
Rockchip BSP names the property so.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/iommu/rockchip,iommu.yaml          | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/rockchip,iommu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/rockchip,iommu.yaml
index 6ce41d1..bb7a33b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/rockchip,iommu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/rockchip,iommu.yaml
@@ -64,6 +64,13 @@ properties:
       Some mmu instances may produce unexpected results
       when the reset operation is used.
 
+  rockchip,disable-device-link-resume:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/flag
+    description: |
+      Leave the mmu alone on runtime resume and suspend: only its master's
+      attach and detach enable and disable it. The registers of some mmu
+      instances answer only once their master has set itself up.
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
